## Summary
The article states that the top four financial real estate trust companies have a non-performing ratio of 80%. This high ratio is attributed to the impact of non-performing real estate project financing (PF). The situation suggests significant financial distress and potential risks in the real estate investment sector.

## Key Points
- Non-performing ratio reaches 80% for major real estate trust companies.
- Real estate project financing (PF) is the primary cause of the non-performance.
- This indicates substantial financial instability in the real estate financial sector.
- The issue may have broader implications for the financial system and market confidence.


